      {
        "text": "Mishaun Watkins serves on the Lynwood Planning Commission, appointed in 2024, and works as a Community Development Analyst for the City of Santa Ana. She earned a degree in political science from California State University, Dominguez Hills. Her campaign says she wants to restore trust in City Hall, spend taxpayer dollars wisely, and expand affordable housing. It says she pushed to update income limits for rent and utility assistance as a planning commissioner. She supports safe sidewalks and crossings, reliable transit for commuters, and streets designed for people first. She supports affordable housing, clean air, and healthy neighborhoods. Her campaign says her Santa Ana programs reduced the local homeless count by roughly 200 people from 2024 to 2026.",
